Simple python script that uses the Proxmox VE API to provision a new VM: creates the VM, sets CPU/RAM/disk, attaches a cloud-init image or ISO, starts it, waits for the guest agent, sets a root password (or adds your SSH key), grabs the assigned IP, and reboots it into a ready state.

Requirements
- python 3
- requests (pip3 install requests)
- a working Proxmox VE node with API access

Setup
1. edit data_config.json:
   - set proxmox_ip, username, and password for your Proxmox node under api.server_info.proxmox
   - under isos, map a short name to the actual template/image file (must already exist on your Proxmox storage, e.g. /var/lib/vz/template/iso/)
   - the Windows entry is different: it points to a VMID of an existing VM template to clone (see the "info" note in the json file), not a file name
2. make sure the image/ISO files referenced in isos are already uploaded to your Proxmox storage.

Usage
Call create_server_api() from _create_server.py with:
   ios          - key from the isos section in data_config.json
   server_name  - name for the new VM
   node         - Proxmox node name
   ssh_key      - (optional) your public SSH key, added to /root/.ssh/authorized_keys
   storage      - disk size in GB (default 25)
   cpu          - CPU cores (default 1)
   ram          - RAM in GB (default 2)

Returns: vmid, root_password, ip_address, node

Notes
- ISOs are not fully automated (no unattended install), you'll need to configure/install through them yourself after mount.
- data_config.json holds credentials, do not commit your real values, keep this file out of version control or replace with your own before pushing.
